  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through Monday)\nIssued at 1129 PM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nThe southeast CONUS ridge will strengthen toward the middle of \nthe week to near record 500mb heights for this time of year\n(~600dam) with the ridge center drifting back west toward our\narea before it weakens by the weekend. As a result, expect above \naverage warmth and mostly dry weather to continue through the work\nweek. There are low chances for afternoon showers and storms \nWednesday, mainly in the east. Early signals show a weak front \napproaching from the west and increasing clouds and rain/storm \nchances for the weekend. This will cool things off a bit, though \nthere are still no signs of that first true fall- like cold front \nyet.\n\nLacy",
